From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OneFeiFan <3022504358@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] treewide: use copy_page()/clear_page() for whole pages
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This patch consolidates the following patches of the r16 series
(original authors are kept in the attached commit messages):

- 旧 0075：zram: use copy_page for full page copy（Mark-PK Tsai）
- 旧 0076：zsmalloc: use copy_page for full page copy（Mark-PK Tsai）
- 旧 0077：f2fs: use copy_page for full page copy（ztc1997）
- 旧 0078：treewide: Optimize page clearing by replacing memset with clear_page（ztc1997）
- 旧 0079：arm64: Align clear_page() to 16 bytes（Sultan Alsawaf）

Origin: zram、zsmalloc：Mark-PK Tsai 的上游改动，经 ztc1997 2e68e9f9d8、30c861f9c1（旧 0075、0076）；f2fs：ztc1997 a005e0a2eb（旧 0077）；treewide clear_page：ztc1997 5078276692（旧 0078）；arm64 clear_page 对齐：ztc1997 95018d48f0（旧 0079）
Upstream-Status: Mixed（zram/zsmalloc 为上游，其余为 ztc1997）
KABI: none
Depends-On: none
Notes: 旧 0075–0079 合并；clear_page() 的 7 个调用点都已核对为页对齐地址；zram 只改 __zram_bvec_read() 的满页分支
Tested-On: r16（2026-11-01）：完整构建、KMI 门禁（7298 个导出符号，缺失 0，CRC 差异 0；670 个厂商模块 0 失败）、开机

Original commit messages:

----- 旧 0075：zram: use copy_page for full page copy -----
Author: Mark-PK Tsai <mark-pk.tsai@mediatek.com>

Some architectures, such as arm, have implemented optimized copy_page for
full page copying.

Replace the full page memcpy with copy_page to take advantage of the
optimization.

Link: https://lkml.kernel.org/r/20231007070554.8657-1-mark-pk.tsai@mediatek.com
Signed-off-by: Mark-PK Tsai <mark-pk.tsai@mediatek.com>
Reviewed-by: Sergey Senozhatsky <senozhatsky@chromium.org>
Cc: AngeloGioacchino Del Regno <angelogioacchino.delregno@collabora.com>
Cc: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
Cc: Matthias Brugger <matthias.bgg@gmail.com>
Cc: Minchan Kim <minchan@kernel.org>
Cc: YJ Chiang <yj.chiang@mediatek.com>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>

----- 旧 0076：zsmalloc: use copy_page for full page copy -----
Author: Mark-PK Tsai <mark-pk.tsai@mediatek.com>

Some architectures have implemented optimized copy_page for full page
copying, such as arm.

On my arm platform, use the copy_page helper for single page copying is
about 10 percent faster than memcpy.

Link: https://lkml.kernel.org/r/20231006060245.7411-1-mark-pk.tsai@mediatek.com
Signed-off-by: Mark-PK Tsai <mark-pk.tsai@mediatek.com>
Reviewed-by: Sergey Senozhatsky <senozhatsky@chromium.org>
Cc: AngeloGioacchino Del Regno <angelogioacchino.delregno@collabora.com>
Cc: Matthias Brugger <matthias.bgg@gmail.com>
Cc: Minchan Kim <minchan@kernel.org>
Cc: YJ Chiang <yj.chiang@mediatek.com>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>

----- 旧 0077：f2fs: use copy_page for full page copy -----
Author: ztc1997 <dev@ztc1997.com>

----- 旧 0078：treewide: Optimize page clearing by replacing memset with clear_page -----
Author: ztc1997 <dev@ztc1997.com>

----- 旧 0079：arm64: Align clear_page() to 16 bytes -----
Author: Sultan Alsawaf <sultan@kerneltoast.com>

With automatic zeroing of pages upon allocation enabled, time spent in
clear_page() is significant according to perf top. Since clear_page() is
used in loops, align it to 16 bytes, which significantly reduces CPU time
spent in clear_page()

Signed-off-by: Sultan Alsawaf <sultan@kerneltoast.com>
---
 arch/arm64/lib/clear_page.S                      | 1 +
 arch/arm64/mm/mmu.c                              | 2 +-
 drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c                    | 2 +-
 drivers/staging/android/ion/heaps/ion_cma_heap.c | 2 +-
 fs/ext4/super.c                                  | 2 +-
 fs/f2fs/checkpoint.c                             | 2 +-
 fs/f2fs/compress.c                               | 2 +-
 fs/f2fs/f2fs.h                                   | 2 +-
 fs/f2fs/node.c                                   | 2 +-
 fs/f2fs/segment.c                                | 8 ++++----
 fs/f2fs/segment.h                                | 2 +-
 kernel/trace/tracing_map.c                       | 2 +-
 mm/zsmalloc.c                                    | 2 +-
 13 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/lib/clear_page.S b/arch/arm64/lib/clear_page.S
index 1fd5d790a..931dd4be6 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/lib/clear_page.S
+++ b/arch/arm64/lib/clear_page.S
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
  * Parameters:
  *	x0 - dest
  */
+	.p2align 4
 SYM_FUNC_START_PI(clear_page)
 	mrs	x1, dczid_el0
 	tbnz	x1, #4, 2f	/* Branch if DC ZVA is prohibited */
diff --git a/arch/arm64/mm/mmu.c b/arch/arm64/mm/mmu.c
index 0199c7d6f..d1205fc17 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/mm/mmu.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/mm/mmu.c
@@ -106,7 +106,7 @@ static phys_addr_t __init early_pgtable_alloc(int shift)
 	 */
 	ptr = pte_set_fixmap(phys);
 
-	memset(ptr, 0, PAGE_SIZE);
+	clear_page(ptr);
 
 	/*
 	 * Implicit barriers also ensure the zeroed page is visible to the page
diff --git a/drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c b/drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c
index 488e4b4cc..57dbce22b 100644
--- a/drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c
@@ -1283,7 +1283,7 @@ static int __zram_bvec_read(struct zram *zram, struct page *page, u32 index,
 	src = zs_map_object(zram->mem_pool, handle, ZS_MM_RO);
 	if (size == PAGE_SIZE) {
 		dst = kmap_atomic(page);
-		memcpy(dst, src, PAGE_SIZE);
+		copy_page(dst, src);
 		kunmap_atomic(dst);
 		ret = 0;
 	} else {
diff --git a/drivers/staging/android/ion/heaps/ion_cma_heap.c b/drivers/staging/android/ion/heaps/ion_cma_heap.c
index 6ba7fd84c..e3e795b07 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/android/ion/heaps/ion_cma_heap.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/android/ion/heaps/ion_cma_heap.c
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@ static int ion_cma_allocate(struct ion_heap *heap, struct ion_buffer *buffer,
 		while (nr_clear_pages > 0) {
 			void *vaddr = kmap_atomic(page);
 
-			memset(vaddr, 0, PAGE_SIZE);
+			clear_page(vaddr);
 			kunmap_atomic(vaddr);
 			page++;
 			nr_clear_pages--;
diff --git a/fs/ext4/super.c b/fs/ext4/super.c
index b13130af2..8a5f418b0 100644
--- a/fs/ext4/super.c
+++ b/fs/ext4/super.c
@@ -3958,7 +3958,7 @@ int ext4_calculate_overhead(struct super_block *sb)
 		blks = count_overhead(sb, i, buf);
 		overhead += blks;
 		if (blks)
-			memset(buf, 0, PAGE_SIZE);
+			clear_page(buf);
 		cond_resched();
 	}
 
diff --git a/fs/f2fs/checkpoint.c b/fs/f2fs/checkpoint.c
index 0484229f4..db63f19ef 100644
--- a/fs/f2fs/checkpoint.c
+++ b/fs/f2fs/checkpoint.c
@@ -1405,7 +1405,7 @@ static void commit_checkpoint(struct f2fs_sb_info *sbi,
 
 	f2fs_wait_on_page_writeback(page, META, true, true);
 
-	memcpy(page_address(page), src, PAGE_SIZE);
+	copy_page(page_address(page), src);
 
 	set_page_dirty(page);
 	if (unlikely(!clear_page_dirty_for_io(page)))
diff --git a/fs/f2fs/compress.c b/fs/f2fs/compress.c
index 342185156..87a6d2157 100644
--- a/fs/f2fs/compress.c
+++ b/fs/f2fs/compress.c
@@ -1816,7 +1816,7 @@ void f2fs_cache_compressed_page(struct f2fs_sb_info *sbi, struct page *page,
 	if (!f2fs_is_valid_blkaddr(sbi, blkaddr, DATA_GENERIC_ENHANCE_READ))
 		goto out;
 
-	memcpy(page_address(cpage), page_address(page), PAGE_SIZE);
+	copy_page(page_address(cpage), page_address(page));
 	SetPageUptodate(cpage);
 out:
 	f2fs_put_page(cpage, 1);
diff --git a/fs/f2fs/f2fs.h b/fs/f2fs/f2fs.h
index d1cdc2e4f..138b73fb9 100644
--- a/fs/f2fs/f2fs.h
+++ b/fs/f2fs/f2fs.h
@@ -2709,7 +2709,7 @@ static inline void f2fs_copy_page(struct page *src, struct page *dst)
 	char *src_kaddr = kmap(src);
 	char *dst_kaddr = kmap(dst);
 
-	memcpy(dst_kaddr, src_kaddr, PAGE_SIZE);
+	copy_page(dst_kaddr, src_kaddr);
 	kunmap(dst);
 	kunmap(src);
 }
diff --git a/fs/f2fs/node.c b/fs/f2fs/node.c
index b19ac26c8..e86d726d8 100644
